Simple Maintenance Tips for Homeowners
Although many repairs require professional assistance, homeowners can take a few simple steps to keep their air conditioning systems running smoothly.
Replace Air Filters
Dirty filters restrict airflow and force your AC to work harder. Replacing filters every one to three months improves efficiency and indoor air quality.
Keep the Outdoor Unit Clean
Remove leaves, grass, and debris from around the condenser unit to maintain proper airflow.
Check Thermostat Settings
Sometimes cooling issues are caused by incorrect thermostat settings or weak batteries rather than mechanical failures.
Keep Supply Vents Open
Blocked vents reduce airflow and make it difficult for your system to cool every room evenly.
These small maintenance tasks help reduce wear and improve overall system performance.
